{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And this is the offering, etc.</b> The reason for His saying <b>and this</b>, etc., is perhaps that He intends to say that Israel should not bring an offering of one kind or of three, but they must bring from all the kinds, and they do not fulfill the obligation of the offering for the Tabernacle unless they bring from all the kinds. And this is what He means by ״וְזֹאת״ — to say: besides the obligation to bring, I further command that the offering be from all these kinds together. And the reason is that the preparation of the Tabernacle is not complete when even one of the kinds is missing. And the intention is not that each and every individual of Israel must bring from all of them, but rather that in the aggregate offering of all Israel all the kinds will be present. Or it may mean that they should accept from the donors all thirteen kinds, and not treat lightly one who brings flax or skins, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:12.760884534Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}